[b]Edge Atlas[/b] renders a compact, filtered atlas of the most relevant price levels docked to the visible right edge of your chart — instead of a conventional landscape of lines running the full width of the chart.

[b]What it does[/b]

Calculation modules produce normalized price levels (period references, sessions, pivots, swing Fibonacci, clustered support/resistance, round numbers). A shared registry filters, ranks, and renders them as short rails and right-docked labels that stay anchored to the visible edge of the chart while you zoom or scroll.

[b]Period levels[/b]

[list]
[*]Previous/current Day, Week, and Month High/Low/Close/Open/Midpoint
[/list]

[b]Sessions[/b]

[list]
[*]Asia, London, New York — High/Low/Midpoint, configurable timezone, current or last completed range
[/list]

[b]Pivot points[/b]

[list]
[*]Traditional and Fibonacci methods, Daily/Weekly/Monthly reference period, PP/R1-3/S1-3
[/list]

[b]Swing Fibonacci[/b]

[list]
[*]Retracements and extensions from the latest confirmed pivot-high/pivot-low pair, with a minimum leg size filter in ATR
[/list]

[b]Support and Resistance[/b]

[list]
[*]Confirmed pivots clustered by ATR distance into weighted zones, filtered by touch count and age, with the nearest supports and resistances selected automatically
[/list]

[b]Round numbers[/b]

[list]
[*]Major/Half/Quarter levels with an automatic or manually set step size
[/list]

[b]Display[/b]

[list]
[*]Five presets (Clean, Intraday, Structure, Everything, Custom) plus fully granular per-level switches with tooltips
[*]Distance, priority, count, and side filters shared across all modules
[*]Code / Code + Price / Full name / Full name + Price label content
[/list]

